{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"68bf3ffc-fec0-44c8-ba73-612035526133","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Build a square on each side of a right triangle. The longest side, opposite the right angle, is the hypotenuse.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Pythagorean theorem"},{"op":"diagram","id":"squares","region":"right","primitives":[{"kind":"line","points":[[0.36,0.28],[0.36,0.6],[0.6,0.6],[0.36,0.28]],"stroke":"solid"},{"kind":"rect","from":[0.04,0.28],"to":[0.36,0.6],"stroke":"solid","fill":true},{"kind":"rect","from":[0.36,0.6],"to":[0.6,0.84],"stroke":"solid","fill":true},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.36,0.28],[0.68,0.04],[0.92,0.36],[0.6,0.6]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"outer boundary of the square on the hypotenuse"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.36,0.56],[0.4,0.56],[0.4,0.6]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"right angle marker"},{"kind":"text","at":[0.4,0.43],"content":"4"},{"kind":"text","at":[0.48,0.56],"content":"3"},{"kind":"text","at":[0.53,0.41],"content":"5"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"68bf3ffc-fec0-44c8-ba73-612035526133","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The squares on the two shorter sides have areas nine and sixteen. Together, their area is twenty-five.","ops":[{"op":"point","id":"area9","canvas_id":"squares","at":[0.46,0.73],"label":"9"},{"op":"point","id":"area16","canvas_id":"squares","at":[0.18,0.43],"label":"16"},{"op":"equation","id":"sum","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"3^2+4^2=9+16=25"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What is the area of the square on the side of length five?","expected_gist":"Twenty-five square units, equal to nine plus sixteen."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"68bf3ffc-fec0-44c8-ba73-612035526133","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The hypotenuse square also has area twenty-five. For every right triangle, the two smaller square areas add to the largest square area.","ops":[{"op":"point","id":"area25","canvas_id":"squares","at":[0.64,0.31],"label":"25"},{"op":"equation","id":"example","anchor":{"el":"sum","side":"below","gap":0.07},"latex":"3^2+4^2=5^2"},{"op":"equation","id":"theorem","anchor":{"el":"example","side":"below","gap":0.09},"latex":"a^2+b^2=c^2"},{"op":"text","id":"condition","anchor":{"el":"theorem","side":"below","gap":0.05},"content":"Right triangle; c is the hypotenuse"}],"checkpoint":null}}
